module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_claim_module_red_on_main_with_its_cause_unread

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_claim_module_red_on_main_with_its_cause_unread: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_claim_module_red_on_main_with_its_cause_unread" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "a claim module is red on main and nothing requires it: the required job (v2-bootstrap) evaluates no witness (gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn), so a claim that stopped holding stays red for every later author, and a brief that depends on it inherits a failure it did not cause.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-10-24 (gunbc#14926, quick-pike-815): test.claim.refinement_discharge rdt_a_holding_predicate_admits_holds and rdt_a_violated_predicate_refuses_at_the_site_holds were red on main 1dd3eda5696a. Cause read by a locator claim on srv1: the controls hand-built their application node, so the evaluator refused it GroundingNotDerived and discharge answered refinement_obligation_undischargeable whatever the predicate body. The evaluator reads grounding only on nodes real ingest produced; a hand-built node is not grounded. The controls now discharge directly over an ingested, infer-grounded module.",

    "SPECIMEN, four sites one shape, read at 4e270740af5: dag/test/claim/host/managed_host_boot_witness.dag:1064 calls host_identity_eq, dag/test/claim/machine_intake/machine_intake_bmc_secure_redfish_witness.dag:231 calls dry_read_bmc_account_state, and dag/test/claim/machine_intake/machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.dag:245 and :488 call observer_clock_modeled and bmc_failed_attempt_window. Each of these three files CARRIES an import block, so proximity never binds the name and nothing else does either: the typechecker reports 'effect summary incomplete: call to X ... has no established callee identity, so its effects cannot be joined'. One such diagnostic reddens EVERY claim of the entry, not only the claim whose helper makes the call -- five declared functions of served_lockout came back FAIL on seven diagnostics, six of which sit inside other claims or other helpers entirely. Nothing about the behaviour is wrong, and the entry stays red for the reason this row already states: no required lane typechecks it and its name is enrolled nowhere. RECOGNITION RULE for this shape: an entry whose claims ALL fail on the same closure diagnostic is missing an import, not a behaviour -- read the first no-established-callee-identity line, take the callee's declaring module (grep its fn), and import the name exactly as the sibling witnesses already do; touch no behaviour. The bare-name shape overlaps gunbc.recurring_failure_mode bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution, whose ceiling metric counts unimported-bare-name refusals, but the mechanism differs: there the name binds by proximity in an import-LESS file, here the file has imports, nothing binds the name, and the refusal is the correct outcome of the missing import.",

    "SPECIMEN, the same gap from the other side -- retiring a declaration does not red the lane that would notice: #16280 (69aa6d29ebf) removed lens_registry_v0_fallback_arm_census and lens_registry_v0_languages_consumer_census from v2.lens.registry while src/v2/lens/enforcement/contract.dag went on importing both (:15, :36), went on carrying the two LensContract rows whose entry: fields read them (:174, :361) and went on listing both in data lens_contract_registry (:545, :566), so the module every enforcement closure walks refers to two declarations that exist nowhere. Read at 857fb6270f6 and run there: test.claim.documentary_refs_witness came back 6/6 FAIL on those two lines alone -- name ... not found in module v2.lens.registry (imported by v2.lens.enforcement.contract) -- 262 s wall, 7.5 GiB peak. The blast radius is not the two censuses: that witness covers design_rulings rows, so every PR adding a ruling was blind while this sat, and the retirement PR was green on exactly the mechanism this row names, no required lane typechecking the closure of a claim module that still refers. THE FIX follows the ruling the retirement carried out (gunbc.rung_drop.lens_enforcement_censuses records the corpus-wide lens enforcement censuses as DELETED): the two contracts go with the instruments rather than the instruments being restored. WHAT A GREP BUYS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT: the four names sit in exactly one file at both revisions, the contract module itself; no ruling and no witness names them; and no witness anywhere asserts a literal count of lens contracts or registry entries -- the five readers of the roster assert only derived arithmetic, == 0, > 0, >= 2, and length(xs: coverage_receipts_live()) == (length(xs: lens_contract_registry) - unbound_contract_count()) -- so the deletion is complete without touching a number. What the grep cannot buy is the red itself: only a run over a closure that reaches the module shows it.",
    "SPECIMEN OF THE SAME SHAPE ONE CONE OVER, RECORDED AND NOT FIXED (scope ruled by the lane manager): v2.test.claim.enforcement.lens_module_gate_witness, all 14 of its declared claims, is 0 PASS / 14 FAIL at 600d966c0dc, 22 closure diagnostics, 460 s wall, 10.0 GiB peak, on the same claim_batch binary (1a0ac121a3f4) that carries this cone's RED. Its roots are src/v2/lens/enforcement/inventory.dag:39, :56, :57 unresolved type 'ScopeRoster' and :63 unresolved type 'LensIdV0'; src/v2/lens/enforcement/standing_intent.dag:43:74 function 'qualified_name_from_dotted_string' not found in scope; and the two diagnostics at src/v2/workflow/enforcement_live.dag:144 and :155 are cascades of the first. The closure of documentary_refs_witness reaches exactly contract, receipts, registry and vocab -- none of these files -- so the imports that greened the ruling-reference claims cannot reach this witness. THE CONE BEHIND inventory.dag and standing_intent.dag HAS NOT BEEN PEELED and its depth is UNMEASURED; a static scan over src/v2/lens flags several hundred candidate unbound type references but also lands on modules other lanes report green, so it sizes nothing and is deliberately not cited as a size. What this receipt is for: the mechanism in this row keeps witnesses red on main invisibly, so a red that was found and deliberately left alone goes on the record with its paths, its count and its binary, rather than being dropped.",
    "SPECIMEN, the same shape a fifth time, read and run at 857fb6270f6: dag/test/claim/machine_intake/host_capture_sol_nul_fill_witness.dag:32 calls repeat_string from the helper nul(n: Int) while the file imports std.live_tree, std.types and gunbc.machine_intake.host_capture_envelope only -- std.render_repeat_string_bootstrap, where that function is declared alone, binds nothing there. The refusal attaches to the helper, not to a claim, so the whole entry dies: another lane's behaviour scope over it at 312e47bfeef came back 3/3 FAIL on that one diagnostic. THE CHECK THAT SEES THIS CLASS, stated because the required gate never sees it: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <witness> --functions <one non-claim helper of it> prints the closure diagnostic and refuses that function without executing a route, since the entry-closure typecheck IS the check -- and because that typecheck is module-wide, one selected function surfaces diagnostics sitting in other claims of the same module. A compile-only walk does not see it: --print-entry-closure stops at the loader boundary and prints module names only. Sweep of the rerun set of the lane that found this (49 witness entries) at that revision: seven closures typechecked clean (fleet_host_smbios_observation, fleet_naming, guarantee_stall, integration_concern, ipmi_boot_options_clear_request, ipmi_cipher_suite_argv, mtcollins_firmware_converge) and repeat_string was the only hit; the rest of the set was left untypechecked here by decision, not by evidence. PREDICTOR TRAP, which is why a grep does not stand in for the run: a name absent from the import list is still not a hit when the call is not a call, or when something other than an import binds it. machine_intake_bmc_forced_first_rotation_witness has no import of std.decl_ref yet every decl_ref(...) in it sits in an admit_callers: annotation list rather than a body; std.measure.second_displacement written qualified and haystack.contains written as a method are not bare calls; join, length, contains, string_contains and string_length appear unimported in witnesses whose closure typechecks clean (typed_argv_exec_realization_witness calls string_contains with no import of it and reports no diagnostic), so the kernel binds them without an import edge; and compile_dag_diagnostic_census in machine_intake_prior_life_boundary_forged_probe_witness has only a types-only import of its home module yet runs 5/5 clean. A negative grep proves nothing either way; only the closure typecheck decides.",



    "RECOGNITION RULE: a control whose input is a hand-built Node handed to the evaluator is undischargeable by construction once grounding is required; read the evaluator's first diagnostic behind the refusal (discharge carries it BEHIND refinement_obligation_undischargeable, and diagnostics_fatal_reason is the last diagnostic by design) before concluding anything about the predicate.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the native compiler judging claim modules on the required path, so a red claim refuses a merge rather than waiting for a reader (the capability gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn names).",
    "SPECIMEN, fifth site, one shape: dag/test/claim/runner/runner_slot_provision_witness.dag ran 0 PASS / 39 FAIL on a fresh clone of main (630f621, srv1 rb-dl pack 1f87fbb, verified vs release-bins.manifest); every one of the 39 failed on 'effect summary incomplete: call to runner_slot_member_key ... has no established callee identity'. The file CARRIES a 30-name import block, so proximity never binds a bare name and nothing else does either: four names were used in code but never imported -- runner_slot_member_key and RunnerSlotEnumerationWidthUnresolved (both gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision), string_contains (std.algebra), and the record read as altra_max_m12830_catalog.architecture (extdeps.cpu.ampere). Because one closure diagnostic reddens EVERY claim of the entry, the four surfaced ONE PER RUN -- each hidden name only appeared after the previous was imported -- which is exactly why 'the whole entry is red on one message' is the tell, not one bad claim. Fix: import each from its owner, matching the sibling witnesses (runner_slot_placement_witness imports all four shapes; runner_slot_allocation_witness imports the catalog by name). After the imports the entry executed: 36 PASS / 3 FAIL, and the three that then failed for real reasons were themselves pre-existing (two fabric-carve claims stale against fabric_execution_slot_identities, which moved the carve to srv1-13/14 under operator decisions 2026-09-21 / 2026-09-26 / PR #14316; one real srv1 over-commitment, runner_count 8 against host_memory_admitted_width 7). That a never-executed entry can sit on a fully-green main and hide both stale claims AND a live budget violation is precisely what this row is for: run the entry, read the one diagnostic, do not silence it."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
